CORE
plain_definition.c runtime_caller.c
--replace-call-with-contract f
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[f\.precondition\.2\] line 8 Check requires clause of f in main: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A runtime [static n] minimum that exists only on the contract's declaration is
kept in the contract's generated requires clause when linking with a plain
pointer definition, so contract replacement still checks it.
